.TH PMV 1 "2026-06-27" "PMV" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pmv \- OpenBSD process mitigation viewer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pmv
[\fI--watch\fR]
[\fI--json\fR]
[\fI--help\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
PMV displays per-process security mitigation status on OpenBSD.
It reads kernel process information via the kvm(3) interface
(kernel memory) and shows pledge(2), unveil(2), W^X, chroot,
and ASLR status for each running process.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \--watch
Continuous monitoring mode with live updates.
.TP
.B \--json
Export process mitigation data in JSON format.
.TP
.B \--help
Display this help message and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I .pmv_snapshot
Persistent state file for snapshot tracking.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B 0
on success, 1 on error.
.SH AUTHOR
Jefferson Cesar Antunes
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR kvm (3),
.BR pledge (2),
.BR unveil (2)
